<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">School of the Americas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Western Hemisphere Institute for Security Cooperation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The School of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army training institution for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American military and police officers, founded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal-zone">Panama Canal Zone</a> in 1946. Moved to Fort Benning in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in 1984 under the canal treaties, it was renamed the Western Hemisphere Institute for Security Cooperation in 2001. Critics have long condemned it because some graduates, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega">Manuel Noriega</a>, were later involved in coups and human rights abuses.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/school-of-the-americas.jpg" alt="School of the Americas" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WHINSEC-Seal.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
